# flatpak -- the application runtime this entire chain exists for.
#
# Nineteen recipes precede this one. The reason is a single unguarded line in
# flatpak's own meson.build -- dependency('gpgme', version : '>=1.8.0') -- which
# pulls in gnupg, which pulls in libgcrypt, libksba, libassuan and npth, all on
# libgpg-error. ostree, libarchive, zstd, json-glib, libseccomp, fuse3,
# bubblewrap, xdg-dbus-proxy and dconf are the rest.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/flatpak/flatpak/releases/download/1.16.1/flatpak-1.16.1.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=2b47e8f2d90d35d29339ed78e1a6eabb36eefa9cfa5a5ca3b0d1f27502c43675
SRC_DIR=flatpak-1.16.1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE THREE THAT DEFINE WHAT THIS PACKAGE IS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -Dsystem_helper=disabled. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS 'enabled', and enabling it makes
# polkit a hard dependency -- meson takes polkit-agent-1 as
# required: get_option('system_helper'). polkit is not packaged.
#
# THIS IS NOT A DEGRADED BUILD. flatpak's own common/flatpak-dir.c:
#     if (self->no_system_helper || self->user || getuid () == 0)
#       return FALSE;
# The helper is bypassed entirely for per-user installations and for root. So
# `flatpak --user` is fully functional, and system-wide installs work when run as
# root -- which on the live ISO is every session. What is lost is exactly one
# thing: an unprivileged user modifying the SYSTEM installation without sudo.
# gnome-software is built for this: it probes for the helper and silently sets
# its default scope to per-user when absent.
# Flip this to enabled the day polkit is packaged; nothing else changes.
#
# -Dsystem_bubblewrap=/usr/bin/bwrap and
# -Dsystem_dbus_proxy=/usr/bin/xdg-dbus-proxy. BOTH DEFAULT TO THE EMPTY STRING,
# which means BUILD THE VENDORED SUBPROJECT. Left alone, flatpak compiles its own
# copies of the two programs that enforce the sandbox -- and those copies are
# invisible to tape's dependency graph and to the signed index. They could not be
# enumerated, audited, or updated when either has a CVE. Both are packaged here
# precisely so that cannot happen.
#
# -Dseccomp=enabled. Already the upstream default; named anyway because it is the
# one option in this file that must never be turned off. A sandbox without a
# syscall filter that still calls itself a sandbox is worse than no sandbox,
# because everything downstream reasons about it as though the filter were there.
# CONFIG_SECCOMP and CONFIG_SECCOMP_FILTER are both set in the kernel config, and
# libseccomp is packaged, so there is nothing to trade away.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE 'auto' OPTIONS, EVERY ONE NAMED
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All of these resolve today from what happens to be in the seed. Naming them
# makes the recipe decide instead of the environment.
#
# -Ddconf=enabled       dconf is packaged (it lands just before this one), so
#                       auto would find it. Named so per-app settings migration
#                       is a property of this recipe.
# -Dlibzstd=enabled     zstd is packaged and published. auto would find it and
#                       delta transport would work; without it downloads are
#                       larger and NOTHING REPORTS IT.
# -Dsystemd=disabled    no systemd here. auto resolves off today -- right outcome,
#                       wrong reason -- and this option only ever controlled
#                       libsystemd integration and systemd unit installation.
# -Dmalcontent=disabled not packaged; parental controls are out of scope.
# -Dselinux_module=disabled  no SELinux, and the module is for the system helper
#                       which is disabled anyway.
# -Dgir=disabled        gobject-introspection IS packaged, so auto would build
#                       GIR data. Nothing here consumes it: gnome-software uses
#                       flatpak's C API.
# -Dman=disabled, -Ddocbook_docs=disabled, -Dgtkdoc=disabled
#                       all need xmlto, docbook or gi-docgen, none packaged.
#
# -Dxauth=disabled IS THE ONE THAT WOULD HAVE SLIPPED THROUGH. It defaults to
# 'enabled', not auto, and libXau IS PACKAGED -- so it would link and work. It is
# for forwarding X11 authority into the sandbox, and this distribution has no X
# server and no Xwayland. Disabled because the dependency being available is not
# a reason to take it.
#
# -Dwayland_security_context=enabled. Needs wayland-client, wayland-scanner and
# wayland-protocols >= 1.32; all three are packaged at 1.41. This is the protocol
# that lets a compositor identify which sandbox a client belongs to, so it is
# kept ON deliberately rather than left to auto -- it is a security capability
# and the pieces are already here.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHECKED AND LEFT ALONE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dsandboxed_triggers defaults true and stays true: it runs post-install
#   triggers inside bwrap rather than on the host. Keeping a default that is a
#   security property is still a decision, so it is written down.
# -Dinstalled_tests defaults FALSE here -- the opposite of json-glib, where the
#   same option name defaults true and would ship test binaries. Verified, not
#   passed.
# -Dauto_sideloading defaults false and installs systemd units; irrelevant here.
# -Dprivileged_group defaults 'wheel' and is moot: it only matters to the system
#   helper, which is disabled.
# -Dtests=false is passed; upstream default is TRUE.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsystem_helper=disabled \
-Dsystem_bubblewrap=/usr/bin/bwrap -Dsystem_dbus_proxy=/usr/bin/xdg-dbus-proxy \
-Dseccomp=enabled -Ddconf=enabled -Dlibzstd=enabled \
-Dwayland_security_context=enabled \
-Dsystemd=disabled -Dmalcontent=disabled -Dselinux_module=disabled \
-Dgir=disabled -Dxauth=disabled \
-Dman=disabled -Ddocbook_docs=disabled -Dgtkdoc=disabled -Dtests=false"
